{"schema":"scion.state/2.0","id":"poem_03","num":"03","title":"HOW TO BREAK OFF AN ENGAGEMENT","tagline":"the storm takes everything that was ever called goods","district":"Mirror Thread Bay","color":"#465fb1","src_fps":12,"xsheet_fps":24,"frames":168,"seconds":14.0,"assets":{"cel":"assets/poem_03_cel.webp","rough":"assets/poem_03_rough.webp","masks":"assets/poem_03_masks.webp","atlas":{"cols":12,"rows":14,"cell":[384,216],"count":168},"rough_atlas":{"cols":12,"rows":14,"cell":[256,144],"count":168},"mask_atlas":{"cols":15,"rows":1,"cell":[256,144],"count":15},"video":"../video/poem_03/cartoon.mp4"},"cuts":[114],"dramatic":{"two_seconds_before":"the storm takes everything that was ever called goods. Before frame 1 we are already inside 'ODE TO FOREVER': the city was moving before the camera arrived, so the opening beat is a stimulus already in progress, not a cold start.","causal_chain":["ANTICIPATION","ACTION_EXTREME","CONTACT_OVERSHOOT","SETTLE","SETTLE"],"beats":[{"id":"B01","role":"ANTICIPATION","heuristic":true,"f_in":0,"f_out":33,"dur_src":33,"dur_24":66,"energy":13.681,"camera_speed":0.05,"sign":"time","sign_image":"Time-image","verb":"the body/camera loads against the coming move \u2014 floor against water, earth","movement":"ODE TO FOREVER","line":"Ode to forever \u2014 a tambourine sounds off an empty temple, empty choir stands, empty prayer lines.","key_frame":31,"mask_key":36,"opens_on_cut":false},{"id":"B02","role":"ACTION_EXTREME","heuristic":true,"f_in":33,"f_out":55,"dur_src":22,"dur_24":44,"energy":14.831,"camera_speed":0.043,"sign":"action","sign_image":"Action-image (SAS)","verb":"the move reaches its extreme \u2014 floor against water, earth","movement":"STILL WHOLE","line":"And abandoned baptism pools. It flies in through the rose window \u2014 still whole.","key_frame":52,"mask_key":48,"opens_on_cut":false},{"id":"B03","role":"CONTACT_OVERSHOOT","heuristic":true,"f_in":55,"f_out":87,"dur_src":32,"dur_24":64,"energy":14.58,"camera_speed":0.066,"sign":"reflection","sign_image":"Reflection-image (ASA)","verb":"the move lands and overshoots \u2014 floor against water, earth","movement":"COBWEBS","line":"Pews taken by cobwebs, and doused in disintegration. Spirits have left salvations in opened gift boxes, placed outside the side doors.","key_frame":86,"mask_key":84,"opens_on_cut":false},{"id":"B04","role":"SETTLE","heuristic":true,"f_in":87,"f_out":111,"dur_src":24,"dur_24":48,"energy":14.374,"camera_speed":0.043,"sign":"time","sign_image":"Time-image","verb":"the world settles into the aftermath \u2014 floor against water, cloud","movement":"UNTIL NOTHING REMAINS","line":"It thunders. Then rains until nothing remains. What was once love, now goods \u2014 broken and sealed apart by lightning. Daily breads, soaked and delivered rotted by rain; and blankets, soiled by venomous puppeteers.","key_frame":110,"mask_key":108,"opens_on_cut":false},{"id":"B05","role":"SETTLE","heuristic":true,"f_in":111,"f_out":168,"dur_src":57,"dur_24":114,"energy":4.244,"camera_speed":0.042,"sign":"time","sign_image":"Time-image","verb":"the world settles into the aftermath \u2014 the figure against wall, ceiling, rock","movement":"TWO SETS OF FOOTSTEPS","line":"Ode to the storm ending. Ode to two sets of mud-imprinted footsteps, leading away from what the water kept.","key_frame":116,"mask_key":114,"opens_on_cut":false}],"keys":[{"id":"K01","frame":31,"beat":"B01","role":"ANTICIPATION","silhouette_key":36},{"id":"K02","frame":52,"beat":"B02","role":"ACTION_EXTREME","silhouette_key":48},{"id":"K03","frame":86,"beat":"B03","role":"CONTACT_OVERSHOOT","silhouette_key":84},{"id":"K04","frame":110,"beat":"B04","role":"SETTLE","silhouette_key":108},{"id":"K05","frame":116,"beat":"B05","role":"SETTLE","silhouette_key":114}],"flip_test":{"mean_key_change":0.344,"reads":true,"note":"keys must differ enough to tell the story with no in-betweens"},"staging_topologies":[{"frame":138,"horizon":0.378,"figure_scale":0.128,"negative_space":0.872,"s